"text": " Bookmakers gave Leicester City a 5,000-to-1 chance of winning the Premier League. A year earlier, they'd spent Christmas bottom of the table and only just escaped relegation. Then they hired Claudio Ranieri. Most predictions still had them going down. But Jamie Vardy scored in 11 Premier League games in a row, a new record. Riyad Mahrez danced past defenders. N'Golo Kante won the ball back everywhere. By Christmas, Leicester were top. May 2nd 2016 The players gathered at Vardy's house To watch Chelsea against Tottenham Spurs had to win 2-0 Tottenham at half time Then Chelsea fought back Eden Hazard 2-2 Leicester were champions for the first time In their 132 year history Biggest shock in sport Or can you name a bigger one?",
